<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jama Masjid, Mandu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1454">1454</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Jama Masjid of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mandu">Mandu</a> is a great mosque begun by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoshang-shah">Hoshang Shah</a>, sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malwa">Malwa</a>, and completed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahmud-khalji">Mahmud Khalji</a> in 1454. Built of red sandstone on a high plinth, with large domes and a vast courtyard, it is said to have been modelled on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-mosque">Great Mosque of Damascus</a>. It is regarded as the finest example of the Afghan style of architecture at Mandu.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jama-masjid-mandu.jpg" alt="Jama Masjid, Mandu" width="320" height="186" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Intekhab0731 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Inside_of_Jama_Masjid.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
